-- title:
--   Canonical aliases for the published actual finite-map primitives
-- statement:
--   This interface gives the original construction names to the previously published coordinate, localization and chart-comparison primitives used by the actual order-thirteen finite-map construction. Every declaration is an alias to the specified public inverse-parameter comparison library. For each of the 194 declarations, the alias has the same kernel type as its library target, and each data alias has the same kernel value. The interface introduces no new geometric conclusion. Its downstream consumer is the original single-section finite-algebra basis and actual finite-map-data construction for the integral Picard representation.
-- source:
--   Forwarding interface to public Definitions.Def_MazurTransfer_Order13InverseParameterChartComparison. All 194 original native declarations were independently compared with the public library for universe arity, kernel type equality, and data value equality. Every canonical alias is checked again against that library target. No original mathematical statement or constructor is changed. The imported library retains the original MazurTheorem per-file attribution and Apache-2.0 headers. Vas and contributors.

